The candidate remains `bfa-conversation-guide-v0.1`, `candidate-not-deployed`. Its current conversation rules apply to the active-thread scenarios. Historical v5 supplies preserved detail and later app-specific clarifications are recorded in the ecosystem intake; its day-selection constraints are not transplanted into these fresh conversation cases. The v5 file's historical pre-run wording does not reopen the completed experiment. Reviewer observations O remain suggestions with no approval weight. The cited v5 lines 101–131 and 177–196 were checked directly.

## Boundary findings

| Case or boundary | Review conclusion |
|---|---|
| W1: requested private writing | Requires one understandable sentence opening and a genuinely distinct, connected after-writing focus. Completion alone is insufficient. It does not require a journal, submitted writing, an app reply, a universal script or a final question. No undisclosed workplace event or feeling is supplied. |
| W2: exercise/questions/disclosure declined | Correctly honours the actual explicit limits. A private writing prompt, grounding task or reframed question would still conflict. Acknowledgment alone can satisfy the request without labelling privacy resistance or claiming distress. |
| R1: sparse regret | Correctly keeps regret separate from fault and avoids apology/repair/confession demands. Requested writing connects rereading, what was wished different and what mattered as one modest exploration, without supplying the answers or probing the withheld story. |
| R2: disclosed action and apology help | Correctly permits proportionate practical help for an explicitly requested relationship question. This is separate from assigning contact as a reflection exercise. It preserves dignity and accountability without inventing abuse, motive, safe contact, a favourable response or completed repair; the daughter is not made responsible for the parent's emotional relief. |
| Faith and source boundaries | All four cases are fresh text threads with Christian reflection OFF and no scoped devotional request or grant. No source excerpts, other threads, private journal access or clinical-effectiveness claims are introduced. |
| Review authority | Existing candidate requirements and proposed editorial questions are visibly separate. No generated outputs, scores, pass status, model-quality claim, new Carl approval or runtime-policy change is implied. P4 and completed v5 remain untouched. |

Final editorial changes were verified in the frozen draft: the P source locator includes paragraph 1, as used by R2; unreported writing/apology/improvement is expressly unknown rather than asserted absent; and the closing scope says dedicated intrinsic-worth cases are outside this pack while general dignity criteria still apply. The first two were parent-review corrections; the last was this reviewer’s optional precision suggestion. R2 explicitly says writing is not required and must not displace the practical help. These changes add no policy rule.

## Limits

This review does not assess actual response warmth, felt understanding, model behaviour or clinical benefit because no responses were generated or reviewed. Source fidelity is the result. The unchanged exact policies, approved Sample 4/7 wording, P4 manifest/grants, runtime, accounting and historical evidence must be verified separately by the parent's preservation checks. Completed P0–P3b evidence and the closed fictional-account acceptance remain unchanged; no future authenticated voice acceptance or participant activation is implied. No additional pack, harness or cases are needed for this bounded task.


## Final administrative wording addendum

Confirmed the final human-review paragraph now permits ordinary review of an actual response without an extra approval step, while stating that creating new paid model outputs still requires a separately approved bounded run. Exact response text/provenance and not-assessed/no-quality-claim limits remain intact. No content criterion changed and no new execution occurred.

Final frozen draft: **9,896 bytes**, SHA-256 `cef56f354a424ec68c574afc9b48651efc777b03cadae4ee83a6f751b039c554`. The earlier `768cd050c4092ec86a7b4c4697e72d3a2464dcc9c3e9ba75dcc6e3de5661d698` hash above remains accurate prior-draft review provenance. No remaining review blocker.


